      "id": "s2",
      "concept": "electrochemical corrosion",
      "narration": "Electrochemical corrosion happens when metals react with water and oxygen in the air. This creates an electrochemical cell where one part of the metal becomes an anode and loses electrons, while another part becomes a cathode and is protected. In iron, the anode forms iron ions that react with oxygen and water to form rust.",
