      "id": "s3",
      "concept": "pitting corrosion",
      "narration": "Pitting corrosion happens when a tiny droplet of water or dust traps low oxygen on a metal surface, creating an anode. The surrounding area has more oxygen and becomes a cathode. This forms an electrochemical cell that drives corrosion, leading to deep, small pits that grow quickly.",
