    {
      "id": "s4",
      "concept": "galvanic corrosion",
      "narration": "Galvanic corrosion happens when two different metals are in contact in a moist environment. The metal with lower electrode potential (more negative) becomes the anode and corrodes, while the other is protected as the cathode. For example, steel and copper in a pipe system: steel corrodes, copper stays safe.",
